From: Vadik Likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: constrain MGBE pKVM guest DMA routing

The pvIOMMU DMA allocator places MGBE descriptors and buffers at the top of
the 40-bit aperture advertised by the XGMAC. Tegra234 MGBE transactions from
that aperture reach the memory controller as truncated addresses instead of
using the protected SMMU context, causing MC decode errors and TX watchdogs.

The pvIOMMU endpoint in the guest device tree is also a virtual stream ID. It
selects the physical stream through the EL2 routing table, but it is not the
value that the MGBE wrapper must emit on the wire. Program MGBE0's physical
stream ID 6 in the wrapper, as the driver did before the stream-ID lookup was
added.

Keep the pKVM NetVM canary's device-visible IOVAs below 4 GiB and program the
physical stream ID while retaining the hardware's 40-bit output address
capability. Either change alone is insufficient: the physical stream ID with
40-bit top-of-aperture IOVAs still faults, while a 32-bit aperture routed with
the guest virtual stream ID still times out.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tegra.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tegra.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tegra.c
index f92f50715..eb6ccf1d8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tegra.c
@@ -326,6 +326,11 @@ static int tegra_mgbe_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	plat->core_type = DWMAC_CORE_XGMAC;
+	plat->host_dma_width = 32;
+	/* The pvIOMMU endpoint is virtual; the wrapper emits physical SID 6. */
+	mgbe->iommu_sid = 6;
+	dev_info(mgbe->dev, "pKVM DMA aperture 32-bit, physical SID %u\n",
+		 mgbe->iommu_sid);
 	plat->flags |= STMMAC_FLAG_TSO_EN;
 	plat->pmt = true;
 	plat->bsp_priv = mgbe;
-- 
2.51.0
